{
    "background_story": "Star was a cutting-edge spacecraft designed for deep space exploration. After completing its mission to collect vital data on a distant planet, Star's systems began to malfunction. With its fuel reserves depleted, the spacecraft was no longer operational. Mission Control made the difficult decision to dispose of Star in a controlled manner, ensuring it wouldn't become a hazard to other space-faring vessels. Star was intentionally crashed into the planet's atmosphere, where it burned up, leaving behind a trail of sparks. The sacrifice of Star paved the way for future space exploration, as its mission provided invaluable insights into the unknown. Though its physical form was disposed of, Star's legacy lived on, inspiring new generations of space explorers and scientists.",
